    "_meta": {
        "title": "KRI band truth table (ADR 0026 section 6.1)",
        "purpose": "The shared fixture for App\\Support\\Kri\\KriBandRule (PHP) and resources/js/lib/kri-band.js (browser). Each case is (direction, green, red, value) -> band. tools/kri-band-check.mjs runs every case through the JS mirror; tests/Unit/Kri/KriBandRuleTest runs the same cases through KriBandRule::bandOf(forBoundaries(direction, green, red), value). A null band is the engine's answer, never 'green'.",
        "derivation": "Worked by hand from MeasureThreshold::bandFor() (higher_worse skips a band when value < min or value >= max; lower_worse skips when value <= min or value > max) over the band lists KriMeasureMigrator::bandsFor() builds: higher_worse [green{max G}, amber{min G, max R}, red{min R}], lower_worse [red{max R}, amber{min R, max G}, green{min G}]; a band with neither bound is dropped and fewer than two surviving bands is no rule. NOT generated by running either implementation.",
        "directionSpelling": "The form spelling (higher_is_worse / lower_is_worse), which is what forBoundaries() takes. The engine spelling (higher_worse / lower_worse) is accepted by both implementations and gives the same answers.",
        "frozenEdges": "A value exactly on the red boundary is red in both directions. A value exactly on the green boundary is amber in both directions."
    },
